Notes for the next release.

CachedRowSet is not supported.

Text from the database that starts with "<html>" is checked before it is
displayed in SsLabel, SsTable cells and the items of the combo boxes and
lists; see SsHtml. The default, a checker with Rules.MULTILINE, renders
HTML that only formats text. If the text has anything else, such as an image, a link or
a style, the text is displayed literally, markup and all, and a warning
is logged that names what is not allowed. An application that needs more
can allow it,
    Globals.setOption(SsHtml.class, SsHtmlChecker.get(Rules.MULTILINE.withElements("img").withAttributes("img@src")));
or go back to the old behaviour with SsHtml.pass(); setSsHtml() does it
for one component or one SsTable. See NOTES/SsHtml-design.md.

Tests: a quick run does a fraction of the slowest test cases, those that
mostly check the JDK's label renderer and image decoders, and the fuzz
tests. Full runs are the default and what CI does; set the property
seesaw.test.quick to true for quick local builds, see IDE_SETUP.md.
